  "source_review": {
    "DfxProcess": "CR-0161 is const-reference getter for regs_; setter is in registers.cpp and minidump_dumper/lite_process_dumper call paths. Header has no lock. Those appear to be per-dump object setup/read/report phases, but repository evidence does not prove concurrent invocation exclusion or publication semantics. GetKeyThread has setter/getter as another extra syntax candidate; no A0 tail finding there.",
    "DfxThread": "CR-0162/0163 are stackBuf_ setter/getter. Current CLI matches both exact locations. minidump_dumper writes buffers while assembling dump and reads later while serializing; no member lock. A0 CR-0164 is GetProcessInfo returning processInfo_ pointer and is not matched; shared pointee does not imply wrapper race. Same-object cross-thread overlap not established.",
